    {
        "content": "<p>Eric: your solution as written fails to type check, at least for me:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">failed</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">to</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">synthesize</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">of</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">class</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">Quote</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Name</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">nameLitKind</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>However if I remove the type annotation <code>: NameLit</code> in the second line it seems to work fine.  Thanks - <code>Lean.quote</code> is the magic function I was looking for.  :)</p>",
